abstract:
Objective To evaluate the application of Octopus 101 perimetry GKP (Goldmann Kinetic Perimetry) module in ophthalmology. Methods Sixty-seven eligible patients (107 eyes) who had visual field (VF) loss were included in the study,24 cases (38 eyes) glaucoma,18 cases (21 eyes) anterior ischemic optic neuropathy and 25 cases (48 eyes) hemianopia.The consistency between static and kinetic VFs of the same eye was analyzed in this study,as well as the repeatability of GKP module. Results All 67 patients (average age 50.7±12.7 years,27 males and 40 females) were examined with GKP module vhile visual acuity in the range of 0.3-1.2.The average GKP examination time of glaucoma group,anterior ischemic optic neuropathy group and hemianopia group were 8.43±2.21min,8.52±1.49min,6.89±2.06min respectively.The average isopter area of Ⅲ 4 e were significantly different to isopter area of Ⅰ 4e (P ＜0.001,t-test) in each group.The VF pairs matched as follows:76.32％ (29/38) in glaucoma group,83.33％ (15/18) in anterior ischemic optic neuropathy group and 100％ (48/48) in hemianopia group.The isopter areas on the first and second SKP test (SKP 1 and SKP 2) were calculated and compared,and showed no significant difference (P=0.68,P=0.59).Correlation between SKP 1 and SKP 2 was good for each isopter (P ＜0.001,Pearson correlation). Conclusions GKP module can be used for the diagnosis and follow up of glaucoma,anterior ischemic optic neuropathy and hemianopia with good repeatability.

Key words: 
Perimetry ;  Goldmann ;  Octopus ;  Visual field loss ;
